\section{Correctness Fix History}
\label{sec:fixes}

During development, eleven correctness and performance issues were identified.
Table~\ref{tab:fixes} summarizes the most significant.

\begin{table}[ht] 
\centering
\caption{Correctness and performance fixes during development.}
\label{tab:fixes}
\begin{tabular}{lll}
\toprule
Fix & File & Description \\
\midrule
A & \texttt{gate.hpp}     & Gate column index: \texttt{d1*D+d2} not \texttt{d1+D*d2} \\
B/C & \texttt{gate.hpp}   & sv1/sv2 absorb must not interleave (shared workspace slots) \\
D & \texttt{main.cpp}     & Center site: 0-indexed \texttt{site\_id(nx/2-1, ny/2-1)} \\
E & \texttt{measures.hpp} & Observable BP: $d=3$ (Z) at center, $d=0$ (I) elsewhere \\
F & \texttt{measures.hpp} & BP on a \emph{copy} of messages; in-place corrupts Vidal gauge \\
G & \texttt{measures.hpp} & Bethe edge: $Z_e = \sum_i \mu_{a\to b}[i]\,\mu_{b\to a}[i]$ \\
H & \texttt{gate.hpp}     & Vidal normalization $\sum\lambda^2=1$ prevents float32 overflow \\
I & \texttt{measures.hpp} & Explicit $Z_e$ sign tracking in Bethe partition function \\
J & \texttt{measures.hpp} & Adaptive BP early exit (tol $= 10^{-5}$) \\
K & \texttt{workspace.hpp}& \texttt{svd\_work} sized $D^2\chimax$ not $D\chimax$ (4$\times$ undersize) \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

Fix~K was the most subtle: the rocSOLVER \texttt{SGESVD} bidiagonal scratch buffer
requires $\min(m,n) = \min(k_{1D}, k_{2D}) = \chimax D^2$ elements.
The buffer was sized at $\chimax D$ (a factor of $D=4$ too small), causing GPU
page faults at $\chimax \geq 75$. The fault was invisible at $\chimax=70$ because
that run never reached chi saturation in 20 layers, keeping $k_{1D} < \chimax D^2$
and the overflow landing in already-mapped GPU memory.

\section{Memory Estimator}
\label{app:estimator}

\texttt{estimate\_memory.py} implements the analytic model of
\S\ref{sec:memory_model} and generates four tables:

\begin{description}
  \item[Table~1] Total GPU memory (GB) for $k\times l$ grids
    ($k,l \in [3,12]$) at $\chi \in \{10,20,30,50,70,100,120\}$.
    Entries exceeding 32\,GB are flagged with \texttt{***}.
  \item[Table~2] Breakdown (psi/messages/workspace/measures)
    at $\chi=50$ and $\chi=100$, with maximum $\chi$ for 32\,GB and 80\,GB targets.
  \item[Table~3] Maximum $\chimax$ for MI60, MI100, MI250X, MI300X,
    A100 (40/80\,GB), H100 across all grids (reproduced in Table~\ref{tab:max_chi}).
  \item[Table~4] Per-gate FLOP estimates (QR + SVD + reconstruction GEMM)
    and per-layer TFLOP totals for representative configurations.
\end{description}

